      "snippet": {
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-11T16:45:34Z",
        "channelId": "UCyNh1mOCVsQ90_oTffjfsLg",
        "title": "The Ghost Ship That Sailed Itself | Dark Chapters",
        "description": "On December 4, 1872, the Dei Gratia found a brigantine sailing the Atlantic with no one aboard. Sails set, cargo of 1,701 barrels of alcohol intact, provisions ample — and the last log entry nine days old. In those nine days, the Mary Celeste had sailed herself nearly 400 nautical miles at under two knots, with no living hand on the wheel. Ten people were aboard: Captain Benjamin Briggs, his wife Sarah, their two-year-old daughter Sophia, and seven crew. None were ever seen again. This is the true story — no invented breakfast on the table — and the science behind the leading theory.\n\nCHAPTERS:\n00:00 The Ship That Sailed Itself\n00:33 Chapter 1: The Family Voyage\n01:20 Chapter 2: The Empty Ship\n02:27 Chapter 3: Nine Days, No Crew\n03:29 Chapter 4: What Happened\n04:19 Chapter 5: The Cursed Ship\n05:00 The Deepest Secret\n\nDark Chapters tells history's darkest true stories — disasters, mysteries and cover-ups they never taught you. New documentary every day.\n\nSpot an error? Let us know in the comments — we correct mistakes.",
