        "title": "The Eruption That Stole a Summer | Dark Chapters",
        "description": "On April 10, 1815, Mount Tambora erupted in Indonesia — the largest eruption in recorded history. It erased two kingdoms overnight, then its ash veil circled the planet and stole the summer of 1816: snow in June, failed harvests, famine on two continents — and, locked indoors by the endless rain, an 18-year-old Mary Shelley wrote Frankenstein.\n\nCHAPTERS:\n00:00 The Kingdom That Vanished\n00:29 Sumbawa, 1815\n01:57 Chapter 2: The Night the Mountain Fell\n03:36 Chapter 3: The Erased Kingdoms\n05:03 Chapter 4: 1816 — The Year Without a Summer\n07:09 Chapter 5: The Frankenstein Summer\n09:26 The Mountain Remains\n\nDark Chapters tells history's darkest true stories — disasters, mysteries and cover-ups they never taught you. New documentary every day.\n\nSpot an error? Let us know in the comments — we correct mistakes.",
